        "original_id": "5738c56a-5204-5989-8894-e80c79d35bd4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2014 Race of Champions, Nations' Cup, individual contest, 24 Hours of Le Mans\n- People: Tom Kristensen, Petter Solberg, David Coulthard, Pascal Wehrlein\n- Places: Bushy Park, Barbados\n\nFacts:\n- From 2000 to 2005, Tom Kristensen won the 24 Hours of Le Mans six consecutive times.\n- Tom Kristensen holds the record for the most wins at the 24 Hours of Le Mans with nine total victories.\n- Later in 2014, Bushy Park in Barbados hosted the 2014 Race of Champions.\n- At the 2014 Race of Champions, the Nordic team of Tom Kristensen and Petter Solberg won the Nations' Cup.\n- At the 2014 Race of Champions, David Coulthard won the individual contest by defeating Pascal Wehrlein 2–0 in the final.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
